<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Iittala</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1881</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Iittala is a Finnish glass and design company, founded in 1881 as a glassworks in the village of Iittala in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/finland">Finland</a>. In the mid-twentieth century designers such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alvar-aalto">Alvar Aalto</a>, Tapio Wirkkala and Timo Sarpaneva made its glassware a symbol of Finnish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/modernism">modernism</a>, and objects such as the Aalto vase of 1936 remain in production under its name.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/iittala.jpg" alt="Iittala" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: iittala group · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Iittala_logo_1.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
